# The project pages moved from /projects to /work. Those paths were indexed,
# listed in the sitemap, and handed to agents as `.md` URLs through /llms.txt
# and the MCP tool output, so they must not start 404ing.
#
# Hand-written rather than declared in astro.config's `redirects`, which is
# where the sitemap and OAuth redirects live. The Cloudflare adapter resolves a
# dynamic destination to the file backing it, so `/work/[slug]` was emitted as
# `/work/:slug/index.html` — not the canonical URL, and a hard 404 for the `.md`
# twins. One splat rule redirects the whole subtree, twins and future slugs
# included, with no per-slug enumeration.
#
# The adapter appends its generated rules to this file rather than replacing it,
# so these stay at the top, and Cloudflare applies the first matching rule.
/projects /work 301
/projects.md /work.md 301
/projects/* /work/:splat 301
